#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124595 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124406 :question/id #uuid "a0246ee6-702f-5d8d-8482-8db1c46b32ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-8295" :question/problem "Given that $w(r, \\theta)=r \\cos 3\\theta,$ find $\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} = \\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial r}\\cos\\theta - \\dfrac{1}{r}\\dfrac{\\partial w}{\\partial \\theta}\\sin\\theta\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }=-3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(-3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879dfc0f-ea2b-5ccb-bbc6-95f43b9c7073" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a66db9c-0ec7-5bff-93d3-e61113901baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478640} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6ab715-8c58-5119-aca6-445e2d5a78d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478641} {:answer/id #uuid "5bacd52a-7451-5471-aa59-d1a60f4350e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478688} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfdc48d-b632-5519-8ba3-19a0e2f15c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478744} {:answer/id #uuid "813ed5fe-e565-55ae-b0a3-dcc8c9821dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a66db9c-0ec7-5bff-93d3-e61113901baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478640} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f8e063-53b4-59b1-a70a-2cbd7cdb3bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c985905c-7d24-536e-9cc0-8e7d7e1b4d34" :question/math-academy-id "q-37186" :question/problem "Given that $w(r,\\theta )=r(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ),$ find $\\frac{∂w}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=\\frac{∂w}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r}=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }=2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a5455a6-a620-598c-ad7d-fe4df9304006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478739} {:answer/id #uuid "be832724-0d5c-5c12-8cac-57e9d7fe56e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478866} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e0ff91-463d-5009-a863-3db111e986e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478879} {:answer/id #uuid "cae67d8e-975c-57a3-acb6-aea452effb82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478883} {:answer/id #uuid "ed302be1-425e-5d43-9c40-6e14e1503e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7e0ff91-463d-5009-a863-3db111e986e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478879} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b6129c-b733-5c71-92b5-462c14e827e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5abfa64-ddd6-5ad1-8a8c-38f9b879752f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95001" :question/problem "Given that $v(r,\\theta )=r(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),$ find $\\frac{∂v}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂v}{∂x}=\\frac{∂v}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $v$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂r}=2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂v}{∂\\theta }=-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5931fbcb-d5d0-514f-9a40-b9dacd7f5ce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282447} {:answer/id #uuid "5b96e589-82a0-56f3-8019-45d38ccf7778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282465} {:answer/id #uuid "9af211ae-d2c1-5419-914b-d99b2a2e61c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283040} {:answer/id #uuid "c7155d84-c3f7-59e4-acae-f39485ce9da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283422} {:answer/id #uuid "e377d96d-2e54-5472-ad65-76a95cf2bbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e377d96d-2e54-5472-ad65-76a95cf2bbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283673} :answer-field/id #uuid "2670f341-82e8-5d70-983c-019cc825c363" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b54313ba-f7d3-5825-b960-2ab13d62a75d" :question/math-academy-id "q-165282" :question/problem "Given that $h(r,\\theta )=r(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1),$ find $\\frac{∂h}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂h}{∂y}=\\frac{∂h}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂r}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta }=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd315d7-b1d5-551a-af37-e14e882123b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358153} {:answer/id #uuid "421e4508-c098-51e8-90e8-98bf10fa5694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358313} {:answer/id #uuid "7d38dabb-3b90-5940-a75d-8510ce424b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358842} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e4c0a7-a55b-5eab-8f76-5e79031a6d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359587} {:answer/id #uuid "d2dd87cb-765e-56e5-b2a7-b887923ea35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1e4c0a7-a55b-5eab-8f76-5e79031a6d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359587} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d594cdf-96e3-59ea-b073-9e09cf2903a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "089e9487-84e2-5cf6-99a6-f3b1375b3cef" :question/math-academy-id "q-95129" :question/problem "Given that $h(r,\\theta )=2r+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ find $\\frac{∂h}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=\\frac{∂h}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂r}=2,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =(2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{2r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5558a820-fe68-5154-b605-abf1888ca002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358495} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccd388d-c735-55eb-b378-f7d1e760c7ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358704} {:answer/id #uuid "7e7beea8-2165-59f1-b2bd-041b16b78155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358854} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb8186e-5270-5422-93d1-cdc25d726dcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359269} {:answer/id #uuid "dbba7a33-6727-5aa3-8d25-973cb0049ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbba7a33-6727-5aa3-8d25-973cb0049ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359678} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf0ec5fc-3755-5a5d-a8d1-a936b1188676" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4ca4975-1827-563d-9fb6-1ff2551b2f31" :question/math-academy-id "q-95130" :question/problem "Given that $g(r,\\theta )={r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta ,$ find $\\frac{∂g}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=\\frac{∂g}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂r}=2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta }=-3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(-3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =r(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52cf3c7c-f856-5e1a-893d-423bede6de59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358463} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6451f3-ba0d-5b74-abb5-e944654eaa92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358982} {:answer/id #uuid "a99fe949-6ed3-526e-8127-1b1ec443989e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359214} {:answer/id #uuid "d2cb342c-cb70-5a1b-b38b-8f594ea8d85e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359595} {:answer/id #uuid "d540cc2e-6105-5828-a5a3-41026567f180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2cb342c-cb70-5a1b-b38b-8f594ea8d85e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359595} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eeefd3d-0951-5ce0-8878-fb3b5684db7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a4e990c-7d6e-5ded-b574-687e77d66cbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-95132" :question/problem "Given that $f(r,\\theta )=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ,$ find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂r}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂r}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂\\theta }=2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\frac{1}{r}(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +2{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a1ee6a-caac-58ee-afb5-38bc8bb1ed51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357819} {:answer/id #uuid "2228fe89-b437-5a7a-aa61-67383a3bc1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358049} {:answer/id #uuid "2486a9ac-6c70-5c04-9668-5c8f9093b469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358077} {:answer/id #uuid "c28adbb2-a46a-5fcd-bc0c-7c33f8291c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta (\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359459} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4bc83b-09f3-5b22-b701-0b449bf034fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta (\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2228fe89-b437-5a7a-aa61-67383a3bc1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358049} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b690a60-fc65-5545-974d-063013346d86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0702360a-d22f-5e34-a49e-3610cfb8aefb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95133" :question/problem "Given that $w(r,\\theta )=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ,$ find $\\frac{∂w}{∂y},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta )$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=\\frac{∂w}{∂r}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂\\theta }=-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "812a2a72-c787-5aec-b20b-53b5609d7060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368880} {:answer/id #uuid "57701b6b-149a-570c-8820-a5a4899a9926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368881} {:answer/id #uui